{"parentUuid":"95204fb8-a73c-4e4b-b096-7fdaaf985331","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a21b9370-2685-47ed-b11e-b7c9dc33e565","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hy43PqEyCrLafd6fVRcURw","type":"tool_result","content":"14:| `data-fps`                   | No            | Optional frame rate hint. CLI render flags can override output fps.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n33:| `data-duration`    | Required for `div` and sub-compositions            | Duration in seconds. An `img` with `data-start` defaults to 3 s; video/audio default to the source length (less the playback offset, over the rate) once known; an authored value trims. Without any resolvable duration the element has no end and stays visible for the rest of the composition.                                                                 |\n35:| `data-media-start` | No                                                 | Offset into the media source, in seconds.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n38:| `data-link`        | No                                                 | Editing contract only (render ignores it): clips sharing an id, e.g. a video and the `<audio>` detached from it in Studio, are edited as one. Keep every member's `data-start`, `data-duration`, `data-media-start` and `data-playback-rate` equal; to unlink, remove the attribute from all members. See [tracks-and-clips.md](tracks-and-clips.md#linked-clips). |\n69:  - **Blast radius — it silences more than the overflow audit.** The attribute is inherited down the subtree (the perception probe walks ancestors), so it also suppresses the rendered-perception checks `text-clipping`, `content-cramped-container`, and `foreground-over-panel` for every descendant. Putting it on a persistent panel that also hosts real foreground content disables collision checks on that content for the panel's whole lifetime. Prefer the narrowest opt-out: scope it to the smallest decorative wrapper, or use per-element `data-layout-bleed=\"true\"` for one intentional primary-text crop. The two canvas/edge checks `primary-offscreen` and `foreground-over-panel` deliberately run **even under** allow-overflow, so it cannot hide a wordmark sliced by the frame or text bleeding onto a panel edge.\n11:## Hard cut\n38:## Trim in/out\n55:## Split / splice\n82:## Duplicate / reuse same source\n109:## Reorder\n136:## Freeze / hold\n144:## Constant speed / slow motion\n162:## Zoom / punch\n170:## Pan / Ken Burns\n183:## Crop / reframe\n191:## Clip-path wipe / reveal / mask / split-screen\n204:## Crossfade\n242:## Volume fades / ducking\n259:## Audio alignment\n320:## Align a sound to an on-screen event\n335:## Copy a group of clips to another time\n370:## Add media (image, video, audio)\n420:## Swap a media file\n437:## Split a section and change its speed\nShell cwd was reset to /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f8f69bc8-024b-4fab-8006-038bde35cf8b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:22:29.967Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"14:| `data-fps`                   | No            | Optional frame rate hint. CLI render flags can override output fps.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n33:| `data-duration`    | Required for `div` and sub-compositions            | Duration in seconds. An `img` with `data-start` defaults to 3 s; video/audio default to the source length (less the playback offset, over the rate) once known; an authored value trims. Without any resolvable duration the element has no end and stays visible for the rest of the composition.                                                                 |\n35:| `data-media-start` | No                                                 | Offset into the media source, in seconds.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n38:| `data-link`        | No                                                 | Editing contract only (render ignores it): clips sharing an id, e.g. a video and the `<audio>` detached from it in Studio, are edited as one. Keep every member's `data-start`, `data-duration`, `data-media-start` and `data-playback-rate` equal; to unlink, remove the attribute from all members. See [tracks-and-clips.md](tracks-and-clips.md#linked-clips). |\n69:  - **Blast radius — it silences more than the overflow audit.** The attribute is inherited down the subtree (the perception probe walks ancestors), so it also suppresses the rendered-perception checks `text-clipping`, `content-cramped-container`, and `foreground-over-panel` for every descendant. Putting it on a persistent panel that also hosts real foreground content disables collision checks on that content for the panel's whole lifetime. Prefer the narrowest opt-out: scope it to the smallest decorative wrapper, or use per-element `data-layout-bleed=\"true\"` for one intentional primary-text crop. The two canvas/edge checks `primary-offscreen` and `foreground-over-panel` deliberately run **even under** allow-overflow, so it cannot hide a wordmark sliced by the frame or text bleeding onto a panel edge.\n11:## Hard cut\n38:## Trim in/out\n55:## Split / splice\n82:## Duplicate / reuse same source\n109:## Reorder\n136:## Freeze / hold\n144:## Constant speed / slow motion\n162:## Zoom / punch\n170:## Pan / Ken Burns\n183:## Crop / reframe\n191:## Clip-path wipe / reveal / mask / split-screen\n204:## Crossfade\n242:## Volume fades / ducking\n259:## Audio alignment\n320:## Align a sound to an on-screen event\n335:## Copy a group of clips to another time\n370:## Add media (image, video, audio)\n420:## Swap a media file\n437:## Split a section and change its speed","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"95204fb8-a73c-4e4b-b096-7fdaaf985331","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"f8f69bc8-024b-4fab-8006-038bde35cf8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuaGTTZ9L1hjGXJYF6JC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0165oEbGCkfcLnfxDX1qXokj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/.claude/skills/hyperframes-core/references && sed -n 11,60p creator-editing-recipes.md; sed -n 136,242p creator-editing-recipes.md; sed -n 437,520p creator-editing-recipes.md","description":"Read trim, speed, zoom, crossfade recipes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_read_input_tokens":159637,"output_tokens":174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1123,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":174,"cache_read_input_tokens":159637,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1123},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0165oEbGCkfcLnfxDX1qXokj":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/.claude/skills/hyperframes-core/references && sed -n 11,60p creator-editing-recipes.md; sed -n 136,242p creator-editing-recipes.md; sed -n 437,520p creator-editing-recipes.md","description":"Read trim, speed, zoom, crossfade recipes"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"hyperframes-core","type":"assistant","uuid":"469f1633-5250-4a8a-a246-645cb6c10c11","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:22:37.062Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d