{"parentUuid":"8cc205b8-7415-4572-973b-04b28a19200e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a21b9370-2685-47ed-b11e-b7c9dc33e565","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SvvquzR8eHpqtLwhkF99RD","type":"tool_result","content":"== fitting\n0.28 0.60 0.64 1.28 6.48 6.52 6.56 6.68 10.24 10.28 10.44 14.08 14.12 14.28 14.32 \n== method\n0.24 \n== archive\n0.44 2.00 2.04 3.16 3.20 3.24 3.28 3.32 3.44 13.12 13.72 13.76 30.92 30.96 31.00 31.04 31.08 31.12 31.16 31.20 31.32 \n== tokens\n0.36 1.08 1.12 1.20 1.24 \n== talk\n0.44 0.56 0.64 0.76 0.84 1.88 5.48 15.72 \n== yours\n0.40 1.32","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e2a17e1b-e6ab-440a-8a2b-47dde44ac2b0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:27:09.099Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== fitting\n0.28 0.60 0.64 1.28 6.48 6.52 6.56 6.68 10.24 10.28 10.44 14.08 14.12 14.28 14.32 \n== method\n0.24 \n== archive\n0.44 2.00 2.04 3.16 3.20 3.24 3.28 3.32 3.44 13.12 13.72 13.76 30.92 30.96 31.00 31.04 31.08 31.12 31.16 31.20 31.32 \n== tokens\n0.36 1.08 1.12 1.20 1.24 \n== talk\n0.44 0.56 0.64 0.76 0.84 1.88 5.48 15.72 \n== yours\n0.40 1.32","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8cc205b8-7415-4572-973b-04b28a19200e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/footage","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"e2a17e1b-e6ab-440a-8a2b-47dde44ac2b0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/footage","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":["/home/diogenes/.t3/userdata/attachments"],"platform":"linux","shell":"bash","osVersion":"Linux 6.19.14-108.fc42.x86_64"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/assets/fonts"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6e3972d7-6abe-4ccc-b636-285b897579b0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:27:09.110Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/footage (was /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/assets/fonts)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour/footage","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"6e3972d7-6abe-4ccc-b636-285b897579b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuadHbZAEDD5otNPo5Q7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tracing the clip's timeline to figure out when each tab click and scene transition happens, mapping the persona switches to roughly 6.5s, 10.24s, and 14.08s marks.\n\nNow I'm structuring the full scene breakdown against the narration timing. Since the brief calls for 90s but the voiceover runs 69.33s, I'll plan to stretch with title and end-card holds, then I'm outlining the opening scene (0–8.7s) with the \"users 25-34\" demographic card being crossed out and replaced by \"A person does,\" followed by the measure scene starting around 8.7s introducing Baste's one-person approach.\n\nFor scene two, I'm mapping phrase timing onto Ren's portrait and a \"measurement sheet\" visual showing films, music, rooms, and pet peeves appearing in sync with each phrase — though I realize I need to check whether persona data actually exists in the personas directory, since it looked empty.\n\nFor the third scene (the \"fitting\" segment, 19.3–27.4s), I'm timing voice pauses against footage where the persona switches between Ren, Ada, and Moss as the voiceover describes the same screen adapting layout, type, color, and motion for each person.\n\nTrying 1.4x instead: that consumes more source material and lands the Moss switch around timeline 26.85, near the scene's end — the cursor would feel hurried but still workable. Let me consider other starting points too.\n\nTesting a 1.15x rate shows Moss, Ren, and Ada all appearing but with Ada only getting about 2.5 seconds on screen, which feels thin. I'm also weighing whether to add a Ken Burns zoom into the garment, given the recorded viewport is 1440×900 against a 1920×1080 composition.\n\nI think framing the footage inside a browser-style window on the pattern paper background is the more designer-appropriate choice, leaving room for captions rather than cropping to fill the frame. Working out the math: a 1440×900 window plus a 36px title bar centered on the 1920×1080 canvas leaves about 72px top and bottom, though I need to check if that's enough space for captions underneath.\n\nAlternatively, I'm considering an editorial split layout — a narrow left column holding a chapter label and a bold phrase, with the footage window sized down on the right. But shrinking the window to around 1296px wide makes UI text inside the footage too small to read comfortably, especially once embedded smaller on the landing page, so that tradeoff concerns me.\n\nSo I think the better path is letting the footage fill most of the frame within a slim window border, and using punch-in zooms during each phrase to draw attention to the relevant region (like the grid in the archive scene or the conversation in the talk scene), possibly with burned-in captions at the bottom.\n\nI'll handle captions myself rather than relying on an existing pipeline — timing phrase-level chunks via silence detection, styling them plain and high-contrast on an ink pill in Instrument Sans, and also exporting a VTT file for the site's track element. The open question is whether to burn in captions given the landing page autoplays muted (where captions matter most), versus relying on the VTT track once the user clicks play with sound on — I want to avoid duplicate captions showing at once.\n\nI'll settle on burning captions into the video as part of the design, styled like a \"basting tape\" strip, and separately provide the VTT as a non-default captions track plus a transcript below the video rather than enabling both simultaneously.\n\nActually, reconsidering the design-focused landing page approach — modern product sites like Linear or Vercel favor clean video with kinetic typography over burned-in captions. I'll go with no burned-in captions, instead using kinetic headline text per scene plus a native VTT captions track and transcript, with poster+play rather than autoplay for the narrated video.\n\nFor the social-sharing consideration, since the destination is the website itself (not external platforms), burned-in captions aren't necessary — sticking with the VTT approach.\n\nNow mapping out segment 4, \"baste,\" with its timing and pause structure: \"To find a direction, Baste tries dozens of loose versions, warm and cool, sparse and dense, and a vision judge looks at every one,\" pairing this with either the contact-sheet/method visual or the archive map filling in.\n\nThe method clip's contact sheet sequence (develop + judge, then the grease-pencil scoring) matches \"tries dozens of loose versions... a vision judge looks at every one\" really well visually. The archive clip is longer, showing the Studio run setup followed by the archive map filling over about 19 seconds, so I'd need to speed that portion up significantly — aiming for roughly 1.5x on setup and 2.5x on the fill to squeeze it into the 9.93s baste scene.\n\nI'm narrowing down the archive timing: skip most of the setup, start just before the \"Cut the assets\" click around 9.5-11.86s, let the archive map appear, then run fast through candidates landing until \"Finished\" around 30.9s. Splitting into Part A (setup/click at 1x, ~4s) and Part B (candidates landing at ~2.9x speed to compress 17s of source into under 6s of timeline), pairing each with voiceover about trying warm/cool, sparse/dense variations.\n\nFor the fit scene (37.3–45.033s), I'm matching \"it keeps the best in each region\" to a visual showing kept drafts circled with grease pencil and starred picks, considering either a method.webm segment from the cut stage or the archive's final zoomed state — leaning toward using method.webm source from roughly 6–16.7s sped up to fit 7.7s of timeline.\n\nMapping out the method clip's phase timing: landing happens early, judge scoring kicks in around the 7.5s mark of source, and the cut/circling/star phase follows near 12.1–16.7s. I'm weighing whether the baste scene should instead pull from the real product archive run showing dozens of loose variants being judged, saving the \"kept best per region\" visual for the fit scene.\n\nFor the cut scene, I'm matching copy to the archive clip's final output panel (\"The cut · 5 assets\") showing hero, background, ambient loop, and icons each scored and downloadable, paired with the tokens.webm showing CSS variables translating across Tailwind and Panda tabs -- timing the \"images,\" \"vector icons,\" \"ambient loops\" lines to specific pause points in the voiceover.\n\nFor the tokens.webm clip, I'm timing it to the \"CSS, Tailwind or Panda\" phrase — starting on CSS variables, then cycling through Tailwind, Panda, and back to CSS as each is named.\n\nFor the fit scene, I need to check the method clip's cut section or the archive map at the end to pick the right frames, so I'll generate a contact sheet to review.\n\nMoving to the talk segment: 54.933–63.9 with voiceover about asking the persona why, paired with talk.webm showing Ren being selected and answering \"What are you into?\" — roughly an 8.97s scene matching a source span of 3.25 to 12.2 at 1x speed, though the clip actually starts on Moss before the click to Ren happens around 3.25+0.7+0.22.\n\nFor the yours segment, 63.9–69.333, the voiceover talks about bringing your own people and cutting something that fits, visualized by yours.webm typing in a persona name and summary — a 5.43s scene stretched via 1.6x rate to cover source 3.54 to 12.2. I'm also trying to figure out the end card: whether it should show the Baste wordmark, the deployed URL (need to check site config/README), and a CLI command like `baste generate <persona-id>` alongside \"Open the Studio.\" I'm thinking of extending the composition about 2.5s past 69.33 to around 72s total so the end card can hold on logo, URL, and command.\n\nNow I'm breaking down exact timing: footage runs 63.9 to about 67.3s where the voice says \"Bring your own people... Measure them in the Studio, and cut something that fits,\" then the end card holds from roughly 67.3 to 73.0s. Beyond that, I'm sketching the measure scene (8.733–19.267) as a designed sequence with no footage — a persona measurement sheet built from real data, three illustrated portraits (Moss, Ren, Ada), focusing on Ren with measurement tags for films, music, rooms, and dealbreakers. Then for the why scene (0–8.733) I'm starting to design a demographic bracket card, a crossed-out stitch motif, and the line \"A person does.\"\n\nWorking through the opening beats: a paper ground with a drafting grid and basting thread line, followed by a generic grey \"persona document\" card showing a typical UX template with \"25–34\" highlighted, which then desaturates and gets struck through with a red basting stitch before dropping away, leading into a bold \"A person does.\" headline with Ren's portrait arriving. Next I want to pull up Ren's actual persona data to populate the measure scene, so I'm searching the personas file for something like \"Chungking\" to find the right entry.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65425,"cache_read_input_tokens":91599,"output_tokens":7637,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7345},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65425,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7637,"cache_read_input_tokens":91599,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65425},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":78082,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"reque