{"parentUuid":"04d9b54d-5cbd-4005-ab42-54ff8abc7c5f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a21b9370-2685-47ed-b11e-b7c9dc33e565","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RjSyjQRGBKDb8PMHEkhbhT","type":"tool_result","content":"== talk\nsilence_start: 1.587211 silence_end: 1.972177 silence_start: 2.599116 silence_end: 2.830159 silence_start: 3.746621 silence_end: 3.996893 silence_start: 4.71161 silence_end: 5.101587 silence_start: 7.409615 silence_end: 7.758367 \n== yours\nsilence_start: 1.106712 silence_end: 1.442018 silence_start: 3.88678 silence_end: 4.205714 \n== measure\nsilence_start: 1.607188 silence_end: 1.971701 silence_start: 3.220907 silence_end: 3.485578 silence_start: 4.701179 silence_end: 4.947937 silence_start: 6.569683 silence_end: 6.944921 silence_start: 8.869297 silence_end: 9.325714 \nwhy Most interfaces are cut for “users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.” Nobody in that bracket has taste. A person does.\nmeasure Baste starts with one person: the films they rewatch, the music they work to, the rooms they feel at home in, and the things they can’t stand in an app.\nfitting Then it fits an interface to them. Same screen, three people. The layout, the type, the colour and the motion all change.\nbaste To find a direction, Baste tries dozens of loose versions, warm and cool, sparse and dense, and a vision judge looks at every one.\nfit It keeps the best in each region, not one winner. So you see the real range of options before anything is final.\ncut What comes out is ready to use: images, vector icons, ambient loops, and design tokens for CSS, Tailwind or Panda.\ntalk And you can ask the persona why. They’ll tell you, in their own words, what they love and what would make a design feel like theirs.\nyours Bring your own people. Measure them in the Studio, and cut something that fits.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f79fd35d-da74-4719-8643-516e8fd69ce3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:38:22.542Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"== talk\nsilence_start: 1.587211 silence_end: 1.972177 silence_start: 2.599116 silence_end: 2.830159 silence_start: 3.746621 silence_end: 3.996893 silence_start: 4.71161 silence_end: 5.101587 silence_start: 7.409615 silence_end: 7.758367 \n== yours\nsilence_start: 1.106712 silence_end: 1.442018 silence_start: 3.88678 silence_end: 4.205714 \n== measure\nsilence_start: 1.607188 silence_end: 1.971701 silence_start: 3.220907 silence_end: 3.485578 silence_start: 4.701179 silence_end: 4.947937 silence_start: 6.569683 silence_end: 6.944921 silence_start: 8.869297 silence_end: 9.325714 \nwhy Most interfaces are cut for “users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.” Nobody in that bracket has taste. A person does.\nmeasure Baste starts with one person: the films they rewatch, the music they work to, the rooms they feel at home in, and the things they can’t stand in an app.\nfitting Then it fits an interface to them. Same screen, three people. The layout, the type, the colour and the motion all change.\nbaste To find a direction, Baste tries dozens of loose versions, warm and cool, sparse and dense, and a vision judge looks at every one.\nfit It keeps the best in each region, not one winner. So you see the real range of options before anything is final.\ncut What comes out is ready to use: images, vector icons, ambient loops, and design tokens for CSS, Tailwind or Panda.\ntalk And you can ask the persona why. They’ll tell you, in their own words, what they love and what would make a design feel like theirs.\nyours Bring your own people. Measure them in the Studio, and cut something that fits.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04d9b54d-5cbd-4005-ab42-54ff8abc7c5f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranc