Type":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"e8e23847-58e4-4e5e-8a0f-8078996b8db8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a21b9370-2685-47ed-b11e-b7c9dc33e565","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01472XwHsqv81x6Q1bLUsJ2X","type":"tool_result","content":"\u001b[90mTranscribe audio/video to word-level timestamps, or import an existing transcript (hyperframes transcribe v0.8.145)\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mUSAGE\u001b[22m\u001b[24m \u001b[36mhyperframes transcribe [OPTIONS] <INPUT>\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mARGUMENTS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n  \u001b[36mINPUT\u001b[39m    Audio/video file to transcribe, or transcript file to import (.json, .srt, .vtt) \u001b[90m(Required)\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mOPTIONS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n            \u001b[36m-d, --dir=<dir>\u001b[39m    Project directory (default: current directory)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n      \u001b[36m-e, --engine=<engine>\u001b[39m    ASR engine: auto (Parakeet if installed and it covers --language, else whisper), parakeet, or whisper. Default: auto. Parakeet is more accurate and faster; install it with `hyperframes models install parakeet`.                                                                                                                                                    \n        \u001b[36m-m, --model=<model>\u001b[39m    Whisper model (default: small.en). Options: tiny.en, base.en, small.en, medium.en, large-v3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n  \u001b[36m-l, --language=<language>\u001b[39m    Language code (e.g. en, es, ja). Whisper transcribes as this language; Parakeet, used when it covers it, detects the language itself.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n                     \u001b[36m--json\u001b[39m    Output result as JSON; progress JSON lines go to stderr \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                  \u001b[36m--to=<to>\u001b[39m    Write an srt or vtt caption sidecar: exported from a transcript file, or written after transcribing audio/video                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \n      \u001b[36m-o, --output=<output>\u001b[39m    Output path for exported SRT/VTT sidecar                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n            \u001b[36m--preserve-cues\u001b[39m    Keep each transcript entry as its own caption cue (skip word-level grouping). Use when exporting an already-cued transcript whose entries have no internal spaces, e.g. single-word or CJK captions. \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                       \n          \u001b[36m--runtime-install\u001b[39m    Allow installing the Whisper runtime. Use --no-runtime-install to require an existing runtime; model downloads remain allowed. \u001b[90m(Default: true)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n       \u001b[36m--no-runtime-install\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \n                 \u001b[36m--optional\u001b[39m    Treat captions as optional: if whisper-cpp is unavailable, skip and exit 0 instead of failing. For pipelines that continue without captions. \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                               \n        \u001b[36m--timeout=<timeout>\u001b[39m    Whisper spawn timeout in ms. Overrides the duration+model auto-scaled default. Increase on slow CPUs (e.g. emulated arm64/x64, low-power laptops) where whisper.cpp takes many seconds per audio second on medium/large models. Applies to the whisper engine only; Parakeet has a separate fixed timeout. Minimum 5000 (5 s). Env: HYPERFRAMES_TRANSCRIBE_TIMEOUT_MS.\n\n\nparakeet parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3  not installed: hyperframes models install parakeet","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f3095f72-a603-4106-9fcc-c0bf3f34cf78","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:43:28.758Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\u001b[90mTranscribe audio/video to word-level timestamps, or import an existing transcript (hyperframes transcribe v0.8.145)\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mUSAGE\u001b[22m\u001b[24m \u001b[36mhyperframes transcribe [OPTIONS] <INPUT>\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mARGUMENTS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n  \u001b[36mINPUT\u001b[39m    Audio/video file to transcribe, or transcript file to import (.json, .srt, .vtt) \u001b[90m(Required)\u001b[39m\n\n\u001b[4m\u001b[1mOPTIONS\u001b[22m\u001b[24m\n\n            \u001b[36m-d, --dir=<dir>\u001b[39m    Project directory (default: current directory)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n      \u001b[36m-e, --engine=<engine>\u001b[39m    ASR engine: auto (Parakeet if installed and it covers --language, else whisper), parakeet, or whisper. Default: auto. Parakeet is more accurate and faster; install it with `hyperframes models install parakeet`.                                                                                                                                                    \n        \u001b[36m-m, --model=<model>\u001b[39m    Whisper model (default: small.en). Options: tiny.en, base.en, small.en, medium.en, large-v3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n  \u001b[36m-l, --language=<language>\u001b[39m    Language code (e.g. en, es, ja). Whisper transcribes as this language; Parakeet, used when it covers it, detects the language itself.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n                     \u001b[36m--json\u001b[39m    Output result as JSON; progress JSON lines go to stderr \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                  \u001b[36m--to=<to>\u001b[39m    Write an srt or vtt caption sidecar: exported from a transcript file, or written after transcribing audio/video                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \n      \u001b[36m-o, --output=<output>\u001b[39m    Output path for exported SRT/VTT sidecar                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n            \u001b[36m--preserve-cues\u001b[39m    Keep each transcript entry as its own caption cue (skip word-level grouping). Use when exporting an already-cued transcript whose entries have no internal spaces, e.g. single-word or CJK captions. \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                       \n          \u001b[36m--runtime-install\u001b[39m    Allow installing the Whisper runtime. Use --no-runtime-install to require an existing runtime; model downloads remain allowed. \u001b[90m(Default: true)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n       \u001b[36m--no-runtime-install\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \n                 \u001b[36m--optional\u001b[39m    Treat captions as optional: if whisper-cpp is unavailable, skip and exit 0 instead of failing. For pipelines that continue without captions. \u001b[90m(Default: false)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                               \n        \u001b[36m--timeout=<timeout>\u001b[39m    Whisper spawn timeout in ms. Overrides the duration+model auto-scaled default. Increase on slow CPUs (e.g. emulated arm64/x64, low-power laptops) where whisper.cpp takes many seconds per audio second on medium/large models. Applies to the whisper engine only; Parakeet has a separate fixed timeout. Minimum 5000 (5 s). Env: HYPERFRAMES_TRANSCRIBE_TIMEOUT_MS.\n\n\nparakeet parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3  not installed: hyperframes models install parakeet","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e8e23847-58e4-4e5e-8a0f-8078996b8db8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
