{"parentUuid":"613096e2-5dbf-428d-9177-0afdd7adcf69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfucEbdN8gXKKha3v4NrV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tormz8NXqVeABn1Pa31ELk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/skills && grep -rn \"flow: \\|storyboard: \\(no\\|yes\\|false\\)\" hyperframes/references/*.md product-launch-video/SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | head -20; grep -rln \"brief contract\" hyperframes/references | head -3","description":"Check the brief field values the workflow expects"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17684,"cache_read_input_tokens":193290,"output_tokens":567,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":387},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17684,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":567,"cache_read_input_tokens":193290,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17684,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17684},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Tormz8NXqVeABn1Pa31ELk":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/skills && grep -rn \"flow: \\|storyboard: \\(no\\|yes\\|false\\)\" hyperframes/references/*.md product-launch-video/SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | head -20; grep -rln \"brief contract\" hyperframes/references | head -3","description":"Check the brief field values the workflow expects"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"hyperframes-core","type":"assistant","uuid":"7d631b85-e6fd-4a29-b389-b060cc83efa1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:48:32.199Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"7d631b85-e6fd-4a29-b389-b060cc83efa1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a21b9370-2685-47ed-b11e-b7c9dc33e565","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tormz8NXqVeABn1Pa31ELk","type":"tool_result","content":"hyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:42:These two are **orthogonal — never merge them into one menu.** All four `flow` × `storyboard` combinations are valid user choices (a companion run runs the same review passes when `storyboard: yes`); a flattened three-option list (\"storyboard review / one shot / companion\") silently makes companion-with-storyboard unselectable. When a diagram or source material summarizes the outcomes as three branches, that is the derived behavior (`brief-contract.md` § 1), not the question shape. In a form-style question UI, keep (a) and (b) as two separate selects.\nhyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:44:Signals replace questions, never add them: an ongoing \"just build it\" / \"surprise me\" / \"don't ask\" locks `flow: automation, storyboard: no`, and every unanswered field becomes a decision with a receipt in the heads-up. A storyboard request, however phrased, locks `storyboard: yes`. Remembered `flow` / `storyboard` values reorder the recommendations — they never make either question disappear. The run's collaborative/autonomous execution mode derives from these two answers — the old first question is never asked; the canonical mapping is `brief-contract.md` § 1.\nhyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:61:Then enter the workflow (`flow: companion` → `/general-video`; otherwise the matched route), installing it first per the SKILL.md's install step. The workflow's Setup writes `BRIEF.md` from this summary as its **first action after `hyperframes init`** (never before — `init` refuses a non-empty directory), using the canonical frontmatter below and preserving the user's important wording in the body — the chosen pitch, when there is one, under `## Intent`. It then records the preference-backed fields (`brief-format.md` names the subset), and asks no brief question again.\nhyperframes/references/review-loop.md:3:How a `storyboard: yes` run earns fidelity one pass at a time: the plan is reviewed as text in chat, the layouts as a sketched `storyboard.html` the user opens in a browser, and the finished piece as the assembled video. Collaborative mode waits at each checkpoint. Autonomous mode posts the same checkpoint summaries and continues, keeping exactly one question before render.\nhyperframes/references/review-loop.md:13:This is a **checkpoint gate** (`brief-contract.md` § 1). A run that starts autonomous normally has `storyboard: no` and does not enter this loop. If mode switches to autonomous mid-run, keep `STORYBOARD.md` current, post the same summary as a heads-up, and continue without waiting; the one kept question comes at § 4.\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:19:**Which keys are memory.** Only the preference-backed subset — `destination`, `aspect`, `language`, `flow`, `storyboard`, `voice`, `style_preset` — is recorded with `media-use` → `scripts/prefs.mjs record` (the store rejects any other key). `style_preset` is stored per workflow: record it with `--workflow <w>` (the store refuses it bare — a look confirmed for one genre is not a default for the others). `message`, `audience`, `length`, `angle` live in the frontmatter only: they describe this video, not the user.\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:45:workflow: faceless-explainer\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:46:flow: automation\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:47:storyboard: yes\nhyperframes/references/brief-contract.md:33:- An ongoing signal such as “surprise me”, “decide for me”, “just build it”, or “stop asking” sets `flow: automation`, `storyboard: no`, and therefore `mode: autonomous` when it appears during intent capture.\nproduct-launch-video/SKILL.md:22:Workflow: Step 0 setup -> `hyperframes.json`; Step 1 capture -> `capture/`; Step 2 design system -> `frame.md`; Step 3 storyboard/script -> `STORYBOARD.md` and `SCRIPT.md`; Step 3.1 audio -> `audio_meta.json`; Step 4 visual design -> enriched `STORYBOARD.md`; Step 5 frames -> `compositions/frames/NN-*.html` and `index.html`; Step 6 final render -> `renders/video.mp4`.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a27e8658-1814-4f69-b33b-26e0a9194ee7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T01:48:32.246Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"hyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:42:These two are **orthogonal — never merge them into one menu.** All four `flow` × `storyboard` combinations are valid user choices (a companion run runs the same review passes when `storyboard: yes`); a flattened three-option list (\"storyboard review / one shot / companion\") silently makes companion-with-storyboard unselectable. When a diagram or source material summarizes the outcomes as three branches, that is the derived behavior (`brief-contract.md` § 1), not the question shape. In a form-style question UI, keep (a) and (b) as two separate selects.\nhyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:44:Signals replace questions, never add them: an ongoing \"just build it\" / \"surprise me\" / \"don't ask\" locks `flow: automation, storyboard: no`, and every unanswered field becomes a decision with a receipt in the heads-up. A storyboard request, however phrased, locks `storyboard: yes`. Remembered `flow` / `storyboard` values reorder the recommendations — they never make either question disappear. The run's collaborative/autonomous execution mode derives from these two answers — the old first question is never asked; the canonical mapping is `brief-contract.md` § 1.\nhyperframes/references/intent-interview.md:61:Then enter the workflow (`flow: companion` → `/general-video`; otherwise the matched route), installing it first per the SKILL.md's install step. The workflow's Setup writes `BRIEF.md` from this summary as its **first action after `hyperframes init`** (never before — `init` refuses a non-empty directory), using the canonical frontmatter below and preserving the user's important wording in the body — the chosen pitch, when there is one, under `## Intent`. It then records the preference-backed fields (`brief-format.md` names the subset), and asks no brief question again.\nhyperframes/references/review-loop.md:3:How a `storyboard: yes` run earns fidelity one pass at a time: the plan is reviewed as text in chat, the layouts as a sketched `storyboard.html` the user opens in a browser, and the finished piece as the assembled video. Collaborative mode waits at each checkpoint. Autonomous mode posts the same checkpoint summaries and continues, keeping exactly one question before render.\nhyperframes/references/review-loop.md:13:This is a **checkpoint gate** (`brief-contract.md` § 1). A run that starts autonomous normally has `storyboard: no` and does not enter this loop. If mode switches to autonomous mid-run, keep `STORYBOARD.md` current, post the same summary as a heads-up, and continue without waiting; the one kept question comes at § 4.\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:19:**Which keys are memory.** Only the preference-backed subset — `destination`, `aspect`, `language`, `flow`, `storyboard`, `voice`, `style_preset` — is recorded with `media-use` → `scripts/prefs.mjs record` (the store rejects any other key). `style_preset` is stored per workflow: record it with `--workflow <w>` (the store refuses it bare — a look confirmed for one genre is not a default for the others). `message`, `audience`, `length`, `angle` live in the frontmatter only: they describe this video, not the user.\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:45:workflow: faceless-explainer\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:46:flow: automation\nhyperframes/references/brief-format.md:47:storyboard: yes\nhyperframes/references/brief-contract.md:33:- An ongoing signal such as “surprise me”, “decide for me”, “just build it”, or “stop asking” sets `flow: automation`, `storyboard: no`, and therefore `mode: autonomous` when it appears during intent capture.\nproduct-launch-video/SKILL.md:22:Workflow: Step 0 setup -> `hyperframes.json`; Step 1 capture -> `capture/`; Step 2 design system -> `frame.md`; Step 3 storyboard/script -> `STORYBOARD.md` and `SCRIPT.md`; Step 3.1 audio -> `audio_meta.json`; Step 4 visual design -> enriched `STORYBOARD.md`; Step 5 frames -> `compositions/frames/NN-*.html` and `index.html`; Step 6 final render -> `renders/video.mp4`.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d631b85-e6fd-4a29-b389-b060cc83efa1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
